      "message": "yeah, I check all the resources who contain extra in db. It includes: consumer, credential, endpoint, group, policy, project, region ,role, service, token ,trust and user.\n\nNo one return \"extras\" key, except **project**\n\nWhen update a project with some extra data, the response will contain \"extra\" key. For example:\nPATCH /v3/project/{project_id}\n{\n    \"project\":{\n        \"test_key\": \"test_value\"\n    }\n}\n\nthe response is like:\n{\n    \"project\":{\n        \"id\": {project_id},\n        ...\n        \"name\": \"admin\",\n        \"test_key\": \"test_value\"\n        \"extra\" :{\n            \"test_key\": \"test_value\"\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nI think it\u0027s a bug for project update API. The \"extra\" in response body is redundant. But We can\u0027t fix it until we support micro version in Keystone since it will change API behavior.",
